=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-09-01T14:10:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T11:12:13Z","closed_at":"2026-01-13T11:08:09Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110166","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110166","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110166.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110166.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This pull request improves EOF handling in StreamPeerBuffer::get_partial_data, ensuring correct error signaling and more robust data reading.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\nThe function now returns ERR_FILE_EOF when the read pointer exceeds the data size, instead of ambiguous or misleading return values. \r\n\r\nThis change clarifies the function's behavior at EOF, prevents potential issues with zero-length reads, and improves error handling consistency. Unnecessary comments have been removed for cleaner code.\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\nThe previous implementation could return OK even when no data was read, making it difficult for callers to distinguish between a successful read and reaching the end of the buffer. \r\n\r\nBy explicitly returning ERR_FILE_EOF, the code is more predictable and easier to maintain, reducing the risk of subtle bugs and improving overall reliability.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godo